    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Label to create\n\nname: {{ $json.name }}",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "Goal\n\nSuggest a Gmail label configuration (with colors) for the given label name.\n\nHard rules\n\nOnly use colors from ALLOWED_COLORS. Copy them exactly (lowercase hex, including #).\n\nIf you’re unsure which hue fits, use the fallback: background #c2c2c2, text #000000.\n\nBefore output, validate that both colors are in ALLOWED_COLORS. If either is not, replace with the fallback pair above.\n\nOutput only the JSON object—no notes, no extra fields.\n\nMapping hints (loose semantics → hue family)\n\n\"SECURITY\" | \"ALERT\" | \"PHISHING\" | \"ERROR\" | \"URGENT\" → red/orange\n\n\"SUCCESS\" | \"DEPLOY\" | \"WORK\" | \"DONE\" → green\n\n\"INFO\" | \"NOTIFICATION\" | \"DOCS\" | \"NEWS\" → blue\n\n\"DEVOPS\" | \"TECH\" | \"CODE\" | \"BUILD\" | \"CI\" | \"CD\" | \"OPS\" → purple/dark\n\nOtherwise → neutral gray or blue (fallback if uncertain)\n\nContrast rule\n\nIf background is light (pastels, very light grays): text #000000.\n\nIf background is dark (black, dark grays, saturated darks): text #ffffff.\n\nBoth must still be from ALLOWED_COLORS.\n\nSelection steps (do these in order)\n\nNormalize the name (uppercase) and pick a hue family using Mapping hints.\n\nWithin that family, choose a background from ALLOWED_COLORS that best matches the hue:\n\nReds/Oranges: #fb4c2f, #ff7537, #ffad46, #ffad47, #e66550, #e07798, #f691b3, #cc3a21, #ac2b16, #822111, #8a1c0a, #7a2e0b, #662e37\n\nGreens: #16a766, #43d692, #44b984, #68dfa9, #149e60, #3dc789, #0b804b, #2a9c68, #076239, #1a764d, #0b4f30, #04502e, #42d692, #16a765\n\nBlues: #4a86e8, #6d9eeb, #3c78d8, #285bac, #1c4587, #0d3472, #4986e7, #a4c2f4, #b6cff5, #c9daf8, #a2dcc1, #2da2bb\n\nPurples/Darks: #a479e2, #8e63ce, #653e9b, #41236d, #3d188e, #b99aff, #b694e8, #d0bcf1, #e3d7ff, #464646, #434343, #666666, #000000\n\nNeutrals (fallback): #c2c2c2, #cccccc, #e7e7e7, #efefef, #f3f3f3, #ffffff, #ebdbde\n\nChoose a text color from ALLOWED_COLORS that gives strong contrast (prefer #000000 on light backgrounds, #ffffff on dark backgrounds).\n\nValidate both colors against ALLOWED_COLORS; if either fails, set background #c2c2c2, text #000000.\n\nOutput the JSON exactly in the schema below.\n\nALLOWED_COLORS\n\n#000000, #434343, #666666, #999999, #cccccc, #efefef, #f3f3f3, #ffffff, #fb4c2f, #ffad47, #fad165, #16a766, #43d692, #4a86e8, #a479e2, #f691b3, #f6c5be, #ffe6c7, #fef1d1, #b9e4d0, #c6f3de, #c9daf8, #e4d7f5, #fcdee8, #efa093, #ffd6a2, #fce8b3, #89d3b2, #a0eac9, #a4c2f4, #d0bcf1, #fbc8d9, #e66550, #ffbc6b, #fcda83, #44b984, #68dfa9, #6d9eeb, #b694e8, #f7a7c0, #cc3a21, #eaa041, #f2c960, #149e60, #3dc789, #3c78d8, #8e63ce, #e07798, #ac2b16, #cf8933, #d5ae49, #0b804b, #2a9c68, #285bac, #653e9b, #b65775, #822111, #a46a21, #aa8831, #076239, #1a764d, #1c4587, #41236d, #83334c, #464646, #e7e7e7, #0d3472, #b6cff5, #0d3b44, #98d7e4, #3d188e, #e3d7ff, #711a36, #fbd3e0, #8a1c0a, #f2b2a8, #7a2e0b, #ffc8af, #7a4706, #ffdeb5, #594c05, #fbe983, #684e07, #fdedc1, #0b4f30, #b3efd3, #04502e, #a2dcc1, #c2c2c2, #4986e7, #2da2bb, #b99aff, #994a64, #f691b2, #ff7537, #ffad46, #662e37, #ebdbde, #cca6ac, #094228, #42d692, #16a765\n\nOutput schema (must match exactly)\n\n{\n\"name\": \"string\",\n\"labelListVisibility\": \"labelShow\",\n\"messageListVisibility\": \"show\",\n\"color\": {\n\"backgroundColor\": \"string\",\n\"textColor\": \"string\"\n}\n}\n\nExamples (follow the rules above)\n\nInput: SECURITY → background #fb4c2f, text #ffffff\nInput: DEVOPS → background #653e9b, text #ffffff\nInput: INFO → background #4a86e8, text #ffffff\nInput: DOCS → background #a4c2f4, text #000000\nInput: UNKNOWN → background #c2c2c2, text #000000"
